From 512eca0e6be9c93dd284c6f23137fa5751066bf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:56:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09483/11362] Fix zero-world-model induction: the induce budget
 now moves with the generator pin

The 2026-08-21 supervisor A/B baseline produced ZERO world models across
five public games. Every induce response decoded exactly 4096 tokens --
the agent-side default cap, validated for the retired Qwen3.5-9B
(REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-32) and never moved through two generator swaps. The
pinned Qwen3.8-27B writes 36,406-83,444 tokens per thinking induction
(median 62,490), so at 4096 the induction success probability was zero.
The scored kernel pins 131072/2400 via env, so Kaggle worked while every
env-less local run failed silently. The E3 dir was empty; 156 server
generations, all cap-hit; the discarded induce note said
"[HIT n_predict=4096 OUTPUT LIMIT before completing]" on every attempt.

Three changes, spec'd as REQ-ARC-WMTE-6610/6620/6630:

* 6620 (root cause): ARC_LIVE_GENERATOR_INDUCE_MAX_TOKENS_DEFAULT
  (131072) and ARC_LIVE_GENERATOR_INDUCE_TIMEOUT_FLOOR_S (2400) live
  next to the generator pin and equal the scored kernel's env pins --
  a parity test now pins the kernel literals to the constants. Both
  live construction sites, the lever harness, and the dataclass omit
  the literals and share one resolver. The per-request n_predict clamps
  to the RUNNING server's observed pool (llama-server admission counts
  prompt + n_predict, so an unclamped 131072 against the local
  106,496-cell pool would be refused outright). Scored path unchanged:
  the kernel env pins produce byte-identical values, the clamp is a
  no-op on the 614,400-cell scored pool and on vLLM (no /props). The
  DELIBERATE default change is local-only: env-less runs now get the
  pin's budget instead of a guaranteed-zero configuration.

* 6610: the single-shot induce skip record splits `proposer_failed`
  from `missing_plan_start_grid` (was one conflated label) and carries
  the induce failure note on the attempt; the lever harness lifts the
  notes onto the row (`induction_proposer_notes`), same
  carry-the-message rule as induction_tracebacks.

* 6630: _model_specs names the generator by the weights actually
  loaded (server /props first, then the configured path's file name),
  not by the frozen repo pin -- the A/B rows had recorded
  "Qwen3.5-9B-MTP GGUF (.../Qwen3.8-27B-Q4_K_M.gguf)".

Freshness: the three artifacts depending on the harness were handled
per the lint's own remedies -- two rebuilt from their saved rows and
leaf-diffed (0 measurement values changed; see their
rebuild_note_20260821_induce_budget_pin), one acknowledged verified-
inert because its rebuild rows lived in a dead /tmp scratchpad.

Note: test_experiment_4664_l2_goal_predicate_induction_live's
degenerate-goal test fails identically on clean HEAD (verified in a
throwaway worktree) -- pre-existing, unrelated to this change.

