-    "noise_floor_same_config_replicate_note": "SAME-SEED replication. This establishes CAUSAL ATTRIBUTION -- a same-seed difference between two identically-flagged arms can only come from run-to-run variation, so if it is zero then any difference an ablation arm shows IS caused by the flag change. It does NOT bound the variance a win-set comparison generalises over: re-running the same seed is structurally near-deterministic here, so this floor is expected to be 0 and a gate that only asks 'did anything change at all' is weak. The generalisation-relevant floor is `noise_floor_control_across_seeds` below.",
